{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791568850,"nonce":"uE9t0SoCXNBbxcKIG3FdOmrWyPg=","message":"Command buffer landed in blinc_ts 2bbdd70, with blinc_abi ae99a62 (LayoutContext::node, resolving a raw id). CI pins ae99a62 and is green.\n\n- NativeLayout.applyCommands(words: Uint32Array, numbers: Float64Array, strings, brushes) replaces applyProperties. Commands: property write, insertBefore, detach, remove, text (content + style mask), paint (field mask: brush index or solid RGBA, text color, radius, border color/width, opacity, visible, transform, clear) and scroll. Nodes cross as their raw id in two u32 words. Consecutive property writes still apply as one atomic edit; otherwise the first failing command throws and earlier ones stay applied (the host validates tree edits in JS before queueing).\n- Layout (TS) owns the queue (src/native/commands.ts): property writes coalesce per node and id; text, paint and scroll merge per node in place; commands for a node removed earlier in the batch are dropped. It flushes at the end of the tick and before any read or immediate LayoutNode edit. Host writes paint, text (through a before-flush hook, so inherited styles are resolved first) and tree edits into it. LayoutNode's public immediate methods are unchanged and flush the queue first.\n- Paint patches with shadows, filters or masks still go through setPaint immediately (the host never makes them).\n\n**Measured** (2026-10-09, Node 24.2.0, M-series Mac, release addon; node benchmarks/host-frame.mjs: 6,031 host nodes (30 rows of 100 cells, each with a text node); each frame repaints and retexts 300 cells, moves 30 cells between rows, and lays out; calls counted on every NativeLayout/NativeLayoutNode method; median of 31 frames)\n- Before (61bbe6b): 931 native calls per frame (setPaint 300, createBrush 300, setText 300, insertBefore 30, compute 1); 79.0 and 97.5 ms in two runs.\n- After: 2 native calls per frame (applyCommands 1, compute 1); 56.8 and 56.1 ms.\n\n**Not done from the plan**: node creation is still one call per node (it returns the handle); text still crosses as napi Strings (no UTF-16/simdutf); classes, attributes and tags still do not cross, so no atom table yet.","files":null}]}